<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA-MARCH MONTHLY INFLATION.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA-MARCH MONTHLY INFLATION.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuanian CPI rose 0.1 percent</p>
<p>in March compared with February, the statistics department said</p>
<p>on Monday.</p>
<p>In a statement, it said that inflation in the first quarter</p>
<p>was 3.5 percent.</p>
<p>The department provided the index figures for major</p>
<p>categories in the CPI basket:</p>
<p>    - Food products and non alcoholic drinks	  - 99.8</p>
<p>    - Alcohol and tobacco				   - 100.2</p>
<p>    - Footwear and clothes				  - 100.2</p>
<p>    - Rents, water, electricity, gas and other fuel - 100.4</p>
<p>    - Household appliances and operation		- 99.8</p>
<p>    - Medical care and heallth services		 - 100.3</p>
<p>    - Transport						 - 100.2</p>
<p>    - Communication					   - 100.0</p>
<p>    - Education						 - 101.2</p>
<p>    - Recreation and culture				- 100.04</p>
<p>    - Hotels and restaurants				- 101.6</p>
<p>    - Other goods and services			    - 99.95</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
